.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-RAISE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-raise
.Nd focus an app's window, or start the app
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ip
.Ar app
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar command ...
.Nm
.Fl l
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is for a key binding that goes to an app whether or not it's running:
.Bl -bullet
.It
If a window of
.Ar app
is open,
.Nm
focuses it.
.It
If one of its windows has the focus already, it focuses the app's next
window, round to the first, so pressing the key again steps through them.
.It
If none is open, it starts the app: by
.Ar command
if one is given, else by the
.Ic Exec
of the app's
.Pa .desktop
entry, else by running
.Ar app .
It's started through
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
so it's among the desktop's processes, or by
.Nm
itself under another compositor.
.El
.Pp
.Ar app
is matched against each window's app id, the last part of a reverse-DNS
app id
.Pq Ql Nautilus No for Ql org.gnome.Nautilus ,
and the name its app's
.Pa .desktop
entry gives
.Pq Dq WhatsApp Web No for a web app whose app id says nothing :
whole, and as written, unless
.Fl i
or
.Fl p
say otherwise.
.Pp
It sees and focuses windows through wlr-foreign-toplevel-management, as
.Xr patina-hud 1
does, so it works under other wlroots compositors too.
Where the compositor doesn't offer that (GNOME), it only starts the app.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i , -insensitive
Ignore case.
.It Fl p , -partial
Match
.Ar app
anywhere in the app id or the name, so
.Ql -ip telegram
finds
.Ql telegram-desktop_telegram-desktop .
.It Fl l , -list
Print the open windows' app ids and their apps' names, the focused one
marked with
.Ql * ,
to find what to name.
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Alt+B to Firefox, in
.Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
(the default):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[bindings]
"Alt+B" = "patina-raise firefox"
.Ed
.Pp
Telegram and WhatsApp, by part of their names, started from their
.Pa .desktop
entries when they aren't open:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
"Alt+G" = "patina-raise -ip telegram"
"Alt+W" = "patina-raise -ip whatsapp"
.Ed
.Pp
Files, opening a new window when there's none:
.Dl patina-raise -i nautilus -- nautilus --new-window
.Pp
In
.Xr wbindkeys 1 Ns 's
.Pa init.lua :
.Dl bind(\(dqALT+B\(dq, \(dqpatina-raise firefox\(dq)
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-hud 1 ,
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
